ue] [17592186421924 1075 #edb/ref 17592186421922 13194139534450 17592186045417 true] [17592186421924 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534450 17592186045417 true] [17592186421924 1077 "selection" 13194139534450 17592186045417 true] [17592186421924 1078 #edb/ref 17592186421919 13194139534450 17592186045417 true] [17592186421924 1079 #uuid "4c296597-6c06-5bf8-aa85-d5015907d1ee" 13194139534450 17592186045417 true] [17592186421925 1075 #edb/ref 17592186421908 13194139534450 17592186045417 true] [17592186421925 1075 #edb/ref 17592186421909 13194139534450 17592186045417 true] [17592186421925 1075 #edb/ref 17592186421913 13194139534450 17592186045417 true] [17592186421925 1075 #edb/ref 17592186421916 13194139534450 17592186045417 true] [17592186421925 1075 #edb/ref 17592186421918 13194139534450 17592186045417 true] [17592186421925 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534450 17592186045417 true] [17592186421925 1077 "selection" 13194139534450 17592186045417 true] [17592186421925 1078 #edb/ref 17592186421916 13194139534450 17592186045417 true] [17592186421925 1079 #uuid "dafe6fcf-90f7-529a-8290-8d2af8b5a7f5" 13194139534450 17592186045417 true] [17592186421926 1068 #edb/ref 17592186421925 13194139534450 17592186045417 true] [17592186421926 1069 "q-129835" 13194139534450 17592186045417 true] [17592186421926 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534450 17592186045417 true] [17592186421926 1071 "Consider the equation ${y}^{″}-12{y}^{′}+35y=0$ where $y=y(x).$ If $y={e}^{\\lambda x}$ is a solution, then $\\lambda =$" 13194139534450 17592186045417 true] [17592186421926 1072 #uuid "57b50761-0ebc-5773-b974-58926652c62b" 13194139534450 17592186045417 true] [17592186421926 1074 "Assuming $y={e}^{\\lambda x}$ and differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}-12\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+35{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}-12\\lambda +35) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-12\\lambda +35 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n(\\lambda -5)(\\lambda -7)=0,\n$$\n\nand so the solutions of the auxiliary equation  are $\\lambda =5$ or $\\lambda =7.$" 13194139534450 17592186045417 true] [17592186421927 1068 #edb/ref 17592186421924 13194139534450 17592186045417 true] [17592186421927 1069 "q-130122" 13194139534450 17592186045417 true] [17592186421927 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534450 17592186045417 true] [17592186421927 1071 "Given that $y=y(x)$ satisfies the equation ${y}^{″}-6{y}^{′}-7y=0,$ which of the following **cannot** be $y(x)?$" 13194139534450 17592186045417 true] [17592186421927 1072 #uuid "ab1d8df9-7551-58b4-b23c-3a36ae997ae9" 13194139534450 17592186045417 true] [17592186421927 1074 "Assuming $y={e}^{\\lambda x}$ and differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}-6\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}-7{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}-6\\lambda -7) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-6\\lambda -7 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n(\\lambda +1)(\\lambda -7)=0,\n$$\n\nand so the solutions of the auxiliary equation  are $\\lambda =-1$ or $\\lambda =7.$\n\nTherefore, any linear combination of the functions ${e}^{-x}$ and ${e}^{7x}$ is a solution to the original differential equation. \n\nAmong the given options, only ${e}^{6x}+{e}^{7x}$ is not a solution." 13194139534450 17592186045417 true] [17592186421928 1068 #edb/ref 17592186421923 13194139534450 17592186045417 true] [17592186421928 1069 "q-90715" 13194139534450 17592186045417 true] [17592186421928 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534450 17592186045417 true] [17592186421928 1071 "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-7\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+12y=0.\n$$" 13194139534450 17592186045417 true] [17592186421928 1072 #uuid "aecf7af1-6026-52e6-a339-611dfc1550ce" 13194139534450 17592186045417 true] [17592186421928 1074 "Let $y={e}^{\\lambda x}.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}-7\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+12{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}-7\\lambda +12) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}-7\\lambda +12=0.\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda -4)=0,\n$$\n\nand so $\\lambda =3$ or $\\lambda =4.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{3x}+B{e}^{4x}.\n$$" 13194139534450 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-3b840a02-6e20-5e04-b9ba-9bc1e18883f2" 17592186421908 "answer-41908330-21d9-59d9-a0b2-a53e1593c36e" 17592186421909 "answer-43359a46-a31b-5979-b00d-e832c7aab359" 17592186421910 "answer-47caa681-8680-5312-9d36-19b2868656e2" 17592186421911 "answer-4deac328-5c08-5937-b799-6f57cf09acfc" 17592186421912 "answer-4eb31420-e922-5f6e-bedb-6f1ece717ad4" 17592186421913 "answer-646c2a9c-ee6b-59ef-abca-48eaa42e7b25" 17592186421914 "answer-7d5b35fd-08b6-534e-aef6-d64720abed6e" 17592186421915 "answer-7fa54804-bed0-557a-ba9a-e0d7bcc11265" 17592186421916 "answer-8b32650e-a838-5e42-b674-904b88326a9b" 17592186421917 "answer-912dd08d-5db0-5a08-ab81-5772fdca1e70" 17592186421918 "answer-a500bf2b-0bcf-52aa-8621-3db9d47c8